l not be eating a  huge bowl of white rice on its own first  thing in the morning in the Asian  culture white rice is often eaten in  moderation together with lots of  vegetables and also other healthy  sources of protein so the protein fat  and fiber in other foods will greatly  reduce the GI of the entire meal making  the high GI of white rice irrelevant so  you will still feel full and satisfied -  simply put when rice is eaten with other  foods whether or not is brown or white  rice it becomes irrelevant  so the second argument is that brown  rice is high in fiber and protein  compared to white rice so here's a quick  comparison between one cup of cooked  brown rice and white rice as you can see  there isn't a significant difference  between the nutritional values yes it is  important to have fiber and protein as  part of a balanced diet but having brown  rice will not significantly increase  your fiber and protein intake unless if  you were to eat a huge amount so it's  just irrelevant to think that having  brown rice over white rice will  contribute to your overall fiber and  protein intake you can still eat white  rice and meet your daily requirements by  adding lots of vegetables and healthy  protein into the meal for instance one  cup of cooked broccoli has a 5.3 gram of  fiber and raspberries has 8 gram of  fiber the next point is digestibility so  we have spoken about the speed of  digestion and how it's almost the same  now let's talk about your body's ability  to digest a food for most of you you  have no problem digesting where the  brown rice or white rice for some of you  including myself with digestive issues  eating brown rice on a regular basis can  cause constipation bloating gas diarrhea  and even cramps  just think of a brown rice like eating  the whole walnut without removing the  shell yes  there are nutrients on the shell but it  will cost your digestive system to work  a lot harder to break the shell hence  causing in digestion in  case white rice has gone through the  refinement process to remove the husk so  this is a better option if you have  digestive issues because white rice is  easier to digest you can also compare  between raw vegetables or cooked  vegetables to some of you eating raw  vegetables can cause in digestion so the  better option would be grouped  vegetables let's take a look at the  nutritional values especially the  micronutrients of brown and white rice  yup there is no argument that brown rice  it's definitely more nutrient dense than  white rice white rice is basically brown  rice with its outer layers removed and  those outer layers contain  micronutrients but it is very important  to note that those micronutrients will  not have a significant impact on weight  loss weight gain on muscle growth it  still comes down to your overall diet  and also lifestyle nowadays you can even  opt for enriched white rice which means  that they have added back some of the  micronutrients lost during the  refinement process so the question is  which is better white rice or brown rice  if you solely look at nutritional values  then of course the brown rice is the  winner if you look at the price tag  white rice is way cheaper and it has a  longer shelf life if you link it to  weight loss or weight gain choosing  between white rice or brown rice is just  irrelevant the bottom line is you can  choose to eat either brown rice or white  rice or mix them up choose the rice you  prefer and that is good to your  digestion white rice should not get a  bad rap I enjoy both brown rice and  white rice depending on where I am and  what goes with my meal and remember guys  the principle of an Asian diet is  moderation so you shouldn't be consuming  a huge plate of rice and then complain  about weight gain consumer eyes in  moderation with lots of vegetables and  also protein and you can even rotate  with other grains so which do you prefer  white or brown do let me know in the  comments below if you enjoyed